INSTALLATION
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Just  replace  the  old  Galledis  file  with  the new version.  You should
possibly write down your old settings before.

Here are the new settings:

--8<--cut here--
yeschar="y"         /* <- Only change if you localized your BBSText!         */
nochar="n"          /* <- Only change if you localized your BBSText!         */
autoadopt=1         /* <- Auto-adopt? 0=No, 1=First File, 2=Standard pattern */
aocommand="AO"      /* <- Command for Adopt Orphans                          */
aodosdate=0         /* <- Adopt file dates from DOS? 0=No, 1=Yes, 2=Ask      */
aoskipsdfile=1      /* <- Skip short description file prompt? 0=No, 1=Yes    */
                    /*    The next three won't work if this one's disabled!  */
aoanonymous=0       /* <- Adopt anonymously? 0=No, 1=Yes, 2=Ask              */
aoprivate=0         /* <- Adopt as private item? 0=No, 1=Yes, 2=Ask          */
aochangealias=0     /* <- Adopt using another alias? 0=No, 1=Yes, 2=Ask      */
                    /*    The next one won't work if this one's enabled!     */
aoskipaddr=1        /* <- Skip addresse prompt? 0=No, 1=Yes                  */
--8<--cut here--

Change the yeschar and nochar variables only if you localized your BBSText,
eg.   to  use  "j"  (for  "ja")  if you're running a german text.  Also, if
you're  such  a  fanatic  nationalist  and  changed  the  BBSMenu  commands
aocommand  should  be  the command you use instead of "AO" (stupid thought,
anyway!)

autoadopt  can  now  also  be  "2":  in this case Galledis will not add the
first  file  name any longer but just add a Return.  This will let CNet use
its standard adopt pattern ("*").

If  autoadopt  is  "1" the new "ao"-set of options is enabled.  These allow
you  to  have  Galledis answer all of CNet's prompts for the first file, so
that  a  FILE_ID.DIZ  processor you've probably installed can already begin
its work (imagine a huge archive...).

So, let's quickly go through what happens if autoadopt is "1"... some
of the ao-variables have a "2" as option. If you set any of these to this
value, Galledis will not add anything for this and the following questions!
That is, if you set aodosdate=2, don't wonder that you have to manually
answer on all other prompts! This is due to technical restrictions I
originally wanted to solve with Galledis v2.0 until the source went over
the jordan...

So, aodosdate, as its name says, specifies an automatic answer for the
"Adopt using dos dates?" prompt. If you didn't put a "2" here, Galledis
will proceed to the aoskipsdfile variable. If you put a "1" here the
next three prompts are processed, with the "2" option enabled again. If
you set "1" for aochangealias, aoskipaddr will of course not work,
remember?

I think you get the idea... set "aodosdate" to 2 if you don't, this will
effectively disable all the stuff.

All ao-options can be influenced with command line arguments (try "LUP ?"
for the online help) and the more important of them are also displayed in
the configuration display.


